==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Diamond cut history.svg|thumb|right|200px|various facet patterns for diamonds]]
[[Image:Dragonfly_eye_3811.jpg|thumb|right|200px|facets in the compound eye of a dragonfly]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|facette}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfæsɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-facet.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æsɪt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any one of the flat [[surface]]s cut into a gem.
#: {{ux|en|This '''facet''' of the diamond was masterfully cut to enhance its value.}}
# One among many [[similar]] or [[related]], yet still [[distinct]] things.
#: {{synonyms|en|aspect}}
#: {{ux|en|The child's learning disability was only one '''facet''' of the problems contributing to his delinquency.}}
# One of a [[series]] of things, such as [[step]]s in a project.
#: ''We had just about completed the research '''facet''' of the project when the order came to cancel it''.
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} One member of a [[compound eye]], as found in [[insect]]s and [[crustacean]]s.
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A smooth circumscribed surface.
#: ''the articular '''facet''' of a bone''
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Any of the small [[joint]]s at each segment of the [[spine]] that provide stability and help guide motion
# {{lb|en|architectural element}} The narrow [[plane]] [[surface]] between [[fluting]]s of a [[column]]; a [[fillet]].
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[face]] of [[codimension]] 1 of a [[polytope]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[criterion]] that can be used to [[sort]] and [[filter]], such as the colour or size of products in an online store.

